WEBVTT

00:10.490 --> 00:11.200
JUJUTSU KAISEN

00:34.480 --> 00:38.690
JUJUTSU KAISEN
The Culling Game Part 1

01:29.990 --> 01:32.990
Episode 57
Tokyo No. 1 Colony, Part 4

01:35.230 --> 01:41.340
The rules' idea of continuation is
just a cover for the real plan.

01:41.340 --> 01:43.030
Mark my words.

01:43.420 --> 01:45.700
When only the strong remain,

01:45.700 --> 01:47.920
Kenjaku is going to drop
a bomb on the game,

01:47.920 --> 01:51.130
and the Culling Game
will fulfill its purpose.

01:51.710 --> 01:55.320
I don't know what kind of bomb
Kenjaku's going to drop.

01:55.320 --> 01:58.810
But it's going to happen
in the near future.

01:58.810 --> 02:01.120
Maybe even this very moment.

02:01.520 --> 02:05.340
That's why I'm preparing by
gathering strong allies

02:05.340 --> 02:07.320
and stocking up points.

02:07.990 --> 02:09.740
I have a few questions.

02:10.710 --> 02:13.500
I doubt she's that strong.

02:13.500 --> 02:18.360
That woman is bait to lure other Players
here for whatever reason works.

02:18.360 --> 02:21.260
People tend to be less wary
of women, you know.

02:22.060 --> 02:23.410
And when you're done using her,

02:23.410 --> 02:25.620
you can just kill her
for her points, right?

02:27.190 --> 02:28.880
What are you talking about?

02:28.880 --> 02:30.800
I'd never do that.

02:31.550 --> 02:34.870
Reggie-sama is my true knight!

02:34.870 --> 02:38.140
So long as I serve him, he'll protect me!

02:38.520 --> 02:40.270
How naïve and stupid.

02:40.710 --> 02:44.380
Do you and your allies possess at
least 100 points between all of you?

02:45.730 --> 02:47.190
Well, yeah.

02:47.640 --> 02:49.580
A new rule will be added soon.

02:50.360 --> 02:53.210
It'll let Players transfer
points between each other.

02:54.630 --> 02:58.320
Hand over all of your points.

02:58.320 --> 03:00.950
Negotiations have broken down.

03:06.180 --> 03:06.890
He vanished?!

03:09.680 --> 03:10.640
Hey!

03:11.100 --> 03:12.050
Nue!

03:12.800 --> 03:13.710
Whoa!

03:15.140 --> 03:15.980
Hey!

03:16.750 --> 03:18.720
Don't let me see your face again.

03:21.910 --> 03:26.510
Oh. I get it, I get it.

03:27.080 --> 03:30.470
I thought you were being lax,
but you can't kill us, can you?

03:30.470 --> 03:33.630
You want the points we
possess, after all.

03:33.630 --> 03:34.960
But...

03:35.600 --> 03:38.210
if you don't fight to kill,

03:38.210 --> 03:40.960
you'll regret it once you're dead.

04:05.460 --> 04:06.740
Hey!

04:06.740 --> 04:08.820
I'm down here, too!

04:08.230 --> 04:10.730
Iori Hazenoki, Current Points: 35

04:09.350 --> 04:10.450
He dead?

04:19.040 --> 04:20.400
You're okay with this?!

04:23.310 --> 04:24.290
This smell!

04:39.060 --> 04:40.550
Is it over?

04:39.130 --> 04:40.930
Reggie Star, Current Points: 41

04:41.480 --> 04:42.680
Not yet.

04:42.680 --> 04:46.980
He ran into a room before the
explosion, just like you.

04:48.300 --> 04:50.270
Not bad.

04:50.270 --> 04:53.100
But you wore him down a good deal, yeah?

05:00.640 --> 05:02.270
Now you get it, right?

05:03.210 --> 05:05.860
They have no intention of protecting you.

05:08.450 --> 05:11.390
So if you understand that, then get lost.

05:19.020 --> 05:20.790
Give it a rest already.

05:21.780 --> 05:24.830
Then say it.

05:26.010 --> 05:28.670
Reggie-sama said it for me!

05:28.670 --> 05:30.680
He said he'd protect me!

05:30.680 --> 05:32.790
He said he liked me!

05:32.790 --> 05:34.530
So you say it!

05:40.120 --> 05:41.820
Sometimes you run into them—

05:42.660 --> 05:45.060
scumbags like you who are all talk

05:45.630 --> 05:48.650
and no real action.

05:48.650 --> 05:50.970
Thanks for that throw,

05:51.940 --> 05:54.060
but now you're all battered.

05:53.790 --> 05:58.380
Chizuru Hari, Current Points: 28

05:54.460 --> 05:56.980
It wasn't easy climbing
all the way back up here.

05:56.980 --> 05:59.420
Use the stairs, Neanderthal.

05:59.420 --> 06:02.720
Ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong,
ding-dong, ding-dong!

06:02.720 --> 06:07.510
A Player has added a new
rule to the Culling Game!

06:07.510 --> 06:07.870
9: Players shall be able to view the
following information on other players:
name, points, number of
rules added, current Colony.

06:07.870 --> 06:14.020
Rule 10: Players are able to
transfer a number of points
of their choosing to other Players.

06:08.490 --> 06:12.670
Rule 10: Players are able to
transfer a number of points

06:12.670 --> 06:14.800
of their choosing to other Players.

06:15.170 --> 06:17.800
What kind of rule is that?

06:50.910 --> 06:52.060
Max Elephant!

06:54.770 --> 06:56.640
He did it again?!

07:10.120 --> 07:12.680
You bastard! How dare you...

07:18.910 --> 07:21.730
What am I doing?

07:22.500 --> 07:25.260
I'll need more points in the future, too.

07:25.260 --> 07:29.030
But Tsumiki won't be forced to
participate in the killing anymore.

07:29.490 --> 07:30.630
Don't lose your patience.

07:30.630 --> 07:32.380
Believe in the others.

07:32.380 --> 07:34.630
Don't obsess over these guys' points.

07:35.300 --> 07:37.010
All I need to do

07:37.530 --> 07:40.000
is use my full might to brush
away any sparks that fall on me.

07:40.560 --> 07:43.130
You have earned five points.

07:43.640 --> 07:46.950
Man, what a waste of points.

07:46.950 --> 07:50.720
How pathetic, getting killed before
he could even use his technique.

07:52.640 --> 07:54.530
Did Remi drop out?

07:54.530 --> 07:56.720
Even so, it's still two on one.

07:56.720 --> 07:59.860
Damn it, I'm still feeling
that first explosion.

07:59.860 --> 08:01.260
Fleeing is not an option!

08:03.200 --> 08:06.000
Maybe I should use my domain?

08:06.490 --> 08:09.060
But my domain is still incomplete,

08:09.060 --> 08:12.100
so I can't close the barrier
and trap my foe inside.

08:13.210 --> 08:17.440
The worst outcome would be them
running off and making me waste it.

08:21.190 --> 08:23.690
Look out!

08:23.690 --> 08:25.540
...out!

08:25.540 --> 08:26.900
...out!

08:26.900 --> 08:28.780
...out!

08:32.570 --> 08:34.260
Two on one.

08:35.380 --> 08:38.570
Do you really think that's a fair

08:39.210 --> 08:40.910
arrangement?

08:42.100 --> 08:45.270
Do you know what they
call people like you?

08:46.290 --> 08:49.120
That's right! Cowards!

08:49.120 --> 08:51.990
And cowardly attacks won't work on me!

08:52.310 --> 08:53.570
Behold!

08:55.340 --> 08:58.950
Zero damage!

09:40.180 --> 09:42.970
JUJUTSU KAISEN

09:43.900 --> 09:45.980
JUJUTSU KAISEN

09:45.980 --> 09:49.360
Fumihiko Takaba, Current Points: 0

09:46.980 --> 09:49.360
Young boy! I'll help you.

09:49.360 --> 09:51.250
I'm 35 this year,

09:51.250 --> 09:54.980
so one look at someone's face and I can
tell if they're a good or bad per—

09:57.540 --> 09:58.460
What?

09:58.850 --> 10:02.220
You've got quite a bad look to you!

10:03.480 --> 10:04.770
Whatever!

10:04.770 --> 10:07.500
I use a relative grading scale!
Just like schools!

10:07.500 --> 10:09.250
Schools use absolute grading scales.

10:09.850 --> 10:11.570
He did protect me.

10:11.570 --> 10:14.030
So I can trust him for now, right?

10:14.880 --> 10:17.390
What do you make of that, Hazenoki?

10:17.390 --> 10:18.690
I don't know him.

10:18.690 --> 10:20.490
It's faster to just ask.

10:20.490 --> 10:21.560
Hey!

10:21.880 --> 10:23.950
Which type are you?

10:29.190 --> 10:30.900
I get it!

10:30.900 --> 10:32.950
You're asking me

10:33.470 --> 10:35.030
if I'm funny

10:35.420 --> 10:36.910
or not,

10:37.090 --> 10:38.730
aren't you?

10:39.580 --> 10:42.290
I'm not. I'm asking what era—

10:42.290 --> 10:44.240
This costume I'm wearing

10:44.240 --> 10:46.430
is modeled after the hero

10:46.430 --> 10:49.900
who first made me laugh my guts out!

10:49.900 --> 10:51.780
So to honor this costume,

10:51.780 --> 10:54.040
I can't let my jokes fall flat!

10:54.420 --> 11:00.380
Here's a gag I just thought of.
Try using it on your sweetheart.

10:58.180 --> 11:00.890
Curse

11:03.240 --> 11:04.510
Be ready for something!

11:04.520 --> 11:06.650
Curse

11:12.090 --> 11:14.890
"I don't want you as my Wi-Fi!"

11:23.920 --> 11:26.790
What a shitty audience!

11:26.790 --> 11:28.520
There are always jerks like you!

11:28.520 --> 11:31.670
People who forgot how
to laugh in the womb,

11:31.670 --> 11:34.700
and yet always sit at
the front of the venue!

11:34.700 --> 11:36.540
You might be the problem.

11:36.540 --> 11:38.000
Yet even so!

11:38.000 --> 11:39.440
He has the same vibes.

11:39.440 --> 11:41.120
I won't abandon you, either!

11:42.090 --> 11:44.030
Because I'm

11:46.170 --> 11:47.890
an entertainer!

11:54.440 --> 11:55.610
He's fast!

11:55.610 --> 11:57.320
His cursed energy skyrocketed!

11:57.320 --> 11:59.560
The shift in output is massive!

11:59.560 --> 12:01.490
This guy is strong!

12:01.490 --> 12:02.830
Be careful.

12:03.040 --> 12:08.050
I'm an old-school entertainer
who's pro-violence!

12:08.820 --> 12:10.830
Now, what will you do,

12:10.830 --> 12:11.710
young boy?!

12:16.580 --> 12:19.010
We'll split those two up.

12:19.010 --> 12:22.900
That other sorcerer is likely capable
of turning his body parts into bombs.

12:23.280 --> 12:25.560
And he's using the reverse
cursed technique to—

12:26.110 --> 12:27.270
You're too close!

12:27.600 --> 12:28.490
Kogane!

12:28.920 --> 12:29.800
Yes?

12:30.230 --> 12:32.350
Pull up Hiromi Higuruma's information.

12:32.890 --> 12:35.150
Itadori's the one who added that rule.

12:32.900 --> 12:35.150
Search Results

12:32.900 --> 12:35.150
Hiromi Higuruma

12:32.900 --> 12:35.150
Points

12:32.900 --> 12:35.150
Rule Added

12:32.900 --> 12:35.150
Current Colony: Tokyo No. 1

12:35.150 --> 12:36.900
Points

12:37.250 --> 12:39.880
I'm done with this Colony.

12:40.960 --> 12:42.660
If you'll back down, I'll let you go.

12:43.910 --> 12:47.290
Huh?! Where do you think you stand?!

12:47.290 --> 12:51.280
I need to recover the points
I lost from you killing Hari!

12:51.280 --> 12:52.410
Hey, you.

12:52.410 --> 12:53.650
It's Takaba!

12:54.950 --> 12:57.760
If you're going to kill
that bomb bastard,

12:57.760 --> 12:59.320
then if you can,

12:59.320 --> 13:01.710
try to steal his points first.

13:03.230 --> 13:04.710
Okay, young boy.

13:05.100 --> 13:08.300
I accept your request.

13:12.730 --> 13:14.600
But I'm an entertainer.

13:15.440 --> 13:18.600
I'll never do anything that would rob
a person of their ability to smile.

13:18.600 --> 13:20.900
As long as you win, I don't care.

13:28.870 --> 13:30.790
Curse

13:29.370 --> 13:30.790
Sparking!

13:36.310 --> 13:38.090
What a dangerous technique!

13:38.410 --> 13:39.210
Bam!

13:39.380 --> 13:40.440
Time for fireworks!

13:41.080 --> 13:42.470
However,

13:42.470 --> 13:44.670
in variety shows...

13:49.530 --> 13:50.580
He's gone?!

13:52.660 --> 13:54.570
Red is banned.

13:59.860 --> 14:00.970
Don't make light of m—

14:07.380 --> 14:09.720
I'm glad you aren't my enemy, Takaba.

14:10.290 --> 14:13.450
Now there's a line I've
always wanted to hear!

14:14.730 --> 14:16.210
Later, young boy!

14:16.210 --> 14:17.420
Don't die.

14:18.740 --> 14:20.190
Aw.

14:20.190 --> 14:22.240
That guy's dead now.

14:22.240 --> 14:25.930
After that much mockery,
Hazenoki will get serious.

14:25.930 --> 14:28.020
Worry about yourself.

14:28.020 --> 14:29.190
I told you, didn't I?

14:29.190 --> 14:32.180
I've already achieved my
objective in this Colony.

14:32.540 --> 14:35.940
So now I can fight for real.
I won't hold back.

15:16.560 --> 15:17.560
Max Elephant!

15:23.970 --> 15:26.570
You even have one like that?!

16:51.530 --> 16:54.990
You've figured out my
technique, haven't you?

16:54.990 --> 16:58.210
But a water attack is pretty
simplistic, isn't it?

17:03.590 --> 17:06.170
You manifest what's on those receipts,

17:06.170 --> 17:08.320
but that's not exactly right, is it?

17:08.840 --> 17:10.290
You're right.

17:10.290 --> 17:15.110
It's hard to describe, but I'd
call it reenacting contracts.

17:15.110 --> 17:17.970
For example, I can do this, too.

17:17.970 --> 17:20.870
Contractual Re-Creation.

17:24.980 --> 17:26.730
What I just used

17:26.730 --> 17:32.070
was a receipt for a two-night, three-day
stay at the 5-star ryokan, Hoshizoratei,

17:32.070 --> 17:34.360
complete with oil treatment.

17:34.360 --> 17:39.330
In other words, my body is now
as refreshed as it would be

17:39.330 --> 17:44.160
after resting up and relaxing
in a hot spring for two days.

17:44.160 --> 17:46.880
Now, how are you faring in comparison?

17:46.880 --> 17:49.060
You have injuries from our earlier fight,

17:49.060 --> 17:51.460
and you've employed multiple
shikigami at once.

17:51.460 --> 17:53.510
You must be exhausted.

17:53.940 --> 17:56.320
I often employ multiple
shikigami at once.

17:56.320 --> 17:58.090
The problem is that

17:58.090 --> 18:01.440
one of those was Max Elephant,
which I usually use alone.

18:02.700 --> 18:06.580
You can readily draw out and
dismiss your shikigami,

18:06.580 --> 18:10.450
but that's not true once
they're injured, is it?

18:10.450 --> 18:14.080
That's why you won't pull out your dog
that can run, attack, and defend.

18:14.080 --> 18:15.200
Because of that,

18:15.200 --> 18:19.240
you've been forced to use multiple
one-trick shikigami at once.

18:19.240 --> 18:23.790
It's a battle of attrition where neither
of us can use big, high-output moves.

18:23.790 --> 18:25.350
It's futile, see?

18:25.350 --> 18:27.700
You can't kill me.

18:29.790 --> 18:31.090
That's true.

18:31.090 --> 18:32.510
In which case, I'll run.

18:32.720 --> 18:33.900
Hold it.

18:42.740 --> 18:44.570
It won't be that easy.

18:49.360 --> 18:49.900
Mobile Terrace

18:49.940 --> 18:51.360
Monday, November 12th

18:56.290 --> 18:58.760
A community gymnasium?

18:58.760 --> 19:01.880
Did he flee inside?
Or is he luring me in?

19:01.880 --> 19:03.900
I could smoke him out with fire,

19:03.900 --> 19:07.380
but getting into another
chase would be annoying.

19:07.380 --> 19:09.790
Well, what shall I do?

19:11.280 --> 19:13.670
Good. It's just as I imagined.

19:14.180 --> 19:16.080
This is the perfect size.

19:17.180 --> 19:21.510
What do you think you're
planning, you damn brat?

19:22.570 --> 19:25.620
You already have something
set up, don't you?

19:30.620 --> 19:33.640
All sorcerers tell lies.

20:29.710 --> 20:33.410
The things I recreate are like shikigami,

20:33.410 --> 20:36.630
so I can give them simple commands.

20:36.630 --> 20:39.450
Knives normally don't fly, right?

20:40.460 --> 20:44.520
Given your personality, I think it's
pointless to ask, but I will anyway.

20:44.520 --> 20:47.800
If you give me your points,
I'll give you an easy death.

20:48.900 --> 20:52.260
Barrier techniques are
difficult, aren't they?

20:53.320 --> 20:55.250
No matter how long I've tried,

20:55.250 --> 20:58.240
I haven't been able to get the hang
of placing an artificial space

20:58.240 --> 21:00.530
of different size over reality.

21:00.530 --> 21:01.750
Which is why...

21:02.700 --> 21:03.990
No way...

21:05.310 --> 21:08.820
I'm using this gymnasium as-is

21:08.820 --> 21:11.710
to deploy my domain.

21:11.710 --> 21:13.380
He can use that?

21:33.590 --> 21:35.380
Domain Expansion:

21:35.890 --> 21:37.350
Chimera Shadow Garden.

21:41.820 --> 21:44.570
Domain Expansion: Chimera Shadow Garden

21:44.570 --> 21:47.950
He's a sorcerer on that level?!

21:48.470 --> 21:52.450
I never said I didn't have big moves.

23:26.110 --> 23:29.550
Even if it's incomplete,
a domain is still a domain!

23:28.890 --> 23:31.540
I'm pulling out my trump
card and activating it!

23:31.540 --> 23:33.110
Not yet! Endure a little longer!

23:33.110 --> 23:34.030
I acknowledge your strength.

23:34.030 --> 23:35.940
Which of us will get crushed first?!

23:35.940 --> 23:38.430
Get crushed!

23:36.940 --> 23:39.900
Next Episode
Tokyo No. 1 Colony, Part 5
